From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 16:02:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 24/28] isolate: balance class-aware active-JavaScript
 admission

Propagate the backend-owned service class from an admitted degradable query leader into its isolate request and suspended permit. Keep dependency work first, preserve resumptions ahead of new starts within each class, and make protected and degradable floors non-preemptive while allowing unused capacity to be borrowed.

Keep the phase-only behavior when class-aware floors are disabled, reject invalid unlimited-capacity floor configurations, and publish the capacity, occupancy, waiter, and acquisition evidence needed to operate the policy. Update the patch-train documentation so the existing degradable, dependency, queue, deployment-analysis, and scheduled-action descriptions agree on the combined admission contract.

Give typed configuration work a fair queue within the protected JavaScript group. Reserve queue and worker eligibility inside existing shared-base limits, retain dependency precedence and overflow, and keep protected/degradable service floors non-preemptive. Account pending initial waits in the same worker limits and expose the combined protected occupancy directly.

Accept a closed per-call HTTP mutation priority hint, propagate it through request execution metadata, and give high mutations at most two turns before eligible ordinary application demand. Preserve dependency and configuration barriers, existing capacity bounds, cancellation ownership and closed metric labels. Publish the protocol capability and checked OpenAPI contract.
